00:28:02.180 --> 00:28:03.020
I play this game a lot.

00:28:03.360 --> 00:28:05.460
I usually find myself playing the niche games a lot.

00:28:05.460 --> 00:28:06.740
So it's not like,

00:28:07.260 --> 00:28:09.440
it's not like it drove me away from playing the game,

00:28:09.560 --> 00:28:10.560
but I definitely think

00:28:10.560 --> 00:28:12.440
it got to the point where after a while

00:28:12.440 --> 00:28:14.100
it was the one thing I kept noticing

00:28:14.100 --> 00:28:16.100
was, like, oh, now I gotta wait for this thing

00:28:16.100 --> 00:28:17.720
to be exactly where I need it to be.

00:28:18.120 --> 00:28:19.660
And I just don't think we need that in a game

00:28:19.660 --> 00:28:21.360
where, like, you're already trying to figure out

00:28:21.700 --> 00:28:23.180
where do I hit these balls from,

00:28:23.180 --> 00:28:24.040
what angle,

00:28:24.340 --> 00:28:25.780
like, what's my pocket goal?

00:28:26.000 --> 00:28:27.060
And then, like, to have this

00:28:28.200 --> 00:28:29.740
annoying timed power meter

00:28:29.740 --> 00:28:31.360
just didn't seem to be doing it for me.

00:28:31.380 --> 00:28:32.860
I agree that it's not perfect,

00:28:33.080 --> 00:28:34.760
but for me it wasn't as much of a,

00:28:34.760 --> 00:28:36.160
enough of a nuisance

00:28:36.160 --> 00:28:37.280
to bother me that much

00:28:37.280 --> 00:28:38.700
because it is so quick.

00:28:39.060 --> 00:28:39.920
Like, it didn't feel like

00:28:39.920 --> 00:28:42.020
I had to wait too long for it to get to where I wanted it to be.

00:28:42.720 --> 00:28:44.580
But yeah, I definitely think there are ways to improve it.

00:28:45.160 --> 00:28:47.300
But as far as your initial impression

00:28:47.300 --> 00:28:49.480
of having to, like,

00:28:49.560 --> 00:28:50.560
pull back the cursor,

00:28:51.080 --> 00:28:52.280
that's what I thought originally too.

00:28:52.320 --> 00:28:53.520
But I think that would have been

00:28:55.020 --> 00:28:56.620
not quite enough for it

00:28:56.620 --> 00:28:59.460
because it's already easier than real pool

00:28:59.460 --> 00:29:00.640
in the sense that you can

00:29:01.080 --> 00:29:02.380
pick exactly where on the ball

00:29:02.380 --> 00:29:03.680
you want to hit. And you're perfect.

00:29:03.680 --> 00:29:04.500
Like, you don't,

00:29:04.640 --> 00:29:06.080
you'll never do a scratch.

00:29:06.240 --> 00:29:08.300
Right, you'll hit exactly where you want. So then to also hit the power

00:29:08.300 --> 00:29:09.220
exactly, perfectly,

00:29:09.360 --> 00:29:10.280
exactly how much you want

00:29:10.280 --> 00:29:11.500
just doesn't feel like

00:29:11.500 --> 00:29:12.320
in real pool

00:29:12.320 --> 00:29:13.380
you can't just say I'm going to hit it

00:29:13.380 --> 00:29:14.840
with this much power and then do it.

00:29:15.020 --> 00:29:16.620
You have to do something to do it.

00:29:16.680 --> 00:29:18.240
So I feel like there needs to be

00:29:18.240 --> 00:29:19.340
kind of like what your solution

00:29:19.340 --> 00:29:20.560
like making it closer to golf

00:29:20.560 --> 00:29:21.600
something to make it like

00:29:21.600 --> 00:29:23.240
Yeah. It's challenging.

00:29:23.500 --> 00:29:24.720
Another thing that I think

00:29:25.440 --> 00:29:26.700
holds this game back

00:29:26.700 --> 00:29:28.760
and I, I feel like you guys played

00:29:28.760 --> 00:29:29.960
mostly the, this,

00:29:30.300 --> 00:29:32.400
like the, the true single player campaign

00:29:32.400 --> 00:29:33.280
like,

00:29:33.280 --> 00:29:34.440
Yeah. Just the,

00:29:34.440 --> 00:29:37.300
the score based. I wanted to play against somebody

00:29:37.300 --> 00:29:38.260
because I felt like

00:29:38.260 --> 00:29:39.200
it wasn't really pool

00:29:39.200 --> 00:29:40.980
unless there was some competition.

00:29:41.500 --> 00:29:42.980
So I, I did the,

00:29:43.120 --> 00:29:44.480
I did play the CPU.

00:29:44.480 --> 00:29:45.940
I would love to play with you guys

00:29:45.940 --> 00:29:47.080
like in a two player game.

00:29:47.540 --> 00:29:49.640
Yeah. Um, but I played against the computer

00:29:49.640 --> 00:29:51.580
