00:30:22.060 --> 00:30:23.340
to the ball on the other side

00:30:23.340 --> 00:30:25.600
of a barrier and like it,

00:30:25.740 --> 00:30:27.180
that should never be the case

00:30:27.180 --> 00:30:28.080
when it's the computer.

00:30:28.280 --> 00:30:29.260
You know, I'm just thinking like

00:30:29.260 --> 00:30:30.660
how hard that must be

00:30:30.660 --> 00:30:32.460
to program computer AI

00:30:32.460 --> 00:30:33.660
for the NES

00:30:34.260 --> 00:30:35.400
on, in 1980.

00:30:35.680 --> 00:30:37.520
I understand. You know what I'm saying?

00:30:37.560 --> 00:30:38.760
Like you're right completely.

00:30:39.020 --> 00:30:40.160
But like, you know,

00:30:40.260 --> 00:30:41.400
we've been dealing with AI

00:30:41.400 --> 00:30:43.200
in terms of like enemy data

00:30:43.200 --> 00:30:44.220
where it's like, you know,

00:30:44.300 --> 00:30:45.760
in a shmup, it's like the,

00:30:45.760 --> 00:30:46.920
the spaceship comes down,

00:30:47.120 --> 00:30:49.140
is programmed to do a very specific path

00:30:49.140 --> 00:30:50.760
and that's considered like,

00:30:50.860 --> 00:30:52.160
wow, look at like how these,

00:30:52.300 --> 00:30:53.960
look at how these enemy ships behave.

00:30:54.220 --> 00:30:55.500
Or like a Goomba

00:30:55.500 --> 00:30:56.820
in Super Mario Brothers

00:30:56.820 --> 00:30:57.900
just kind of like

00:30:57.900 --> 00:30:58.980
walking from one end

00:30:58.980 --> 00:30:59.820
of the screen to the other

00:30:59.820 --> 00:31:00.820
and being like, oh my gosh,

00:31:00.960 --> 00:31:01.940
I gotta dodge it. Like,

00:31:02.300 --> 00:31:03.380
this is like something where you actually

00:31:03.380 --> 00:31:04.240
have to tell the computer,

00:31:04.440 --> 00:31:05.720
here's all the rules

00:31:05.720 --> 00:31:08.260
to billiards. Here's the best way

00:31:08.260 --> 00:31:09.460
to get certain shots.

00:31:09.820 --> 00:31:10.640
Do this.

00:31:10.780 --> 00:31:11.740
But also don't do it

00:31:11.740 --> 00:31:13.620
too perfect because that would upset you.

00:31:13.620 --> 00:31:15.140
Yeah, it's, but that's true,

00:31:15.340 --> 00:31:16.520
but I also think that

00:31:16.520 --> 00:31:17.620
there's gotta, and I'm,

00:31:17.740 --> 00:31:19.420
again, I'm not a programmer,

00:31:19.680 --> 00:31:21.400
but part of what we do here

00:31:21.400 --> 00:31:22.520
is just criticize stuff.

00:31:22.700 --> 00:31:24.380
We should. There's gotta be

00:31:25.140 --> 00:31:26.360
like some way

00:31:26.360 --> 00:31:27.360
in programming

00:31:27.360 --> 00:31:28.320
to do like an

00:31:28.320 --> 00:31:29.360
if-then statement

00:31:29.360 --> 00:31:31.240
of if the ball,

00:31:31.380 --> 00:31:33.060
the hole is before the ball,

00:31:33.180 --> 00:31:34.320
don't make the shot.

00:31:35.260 --> 00:31:36.620
Right, right, right. Don't make any

00:31:36.620 --> 00:31:37.880
straight pocket shots.

00:31:38.100 --> 00:31:39.760
Yeah. I do think there's,

00:31:39.860 --> 00:31:40.880
I can't remember the game,

00:31:41.040 --> 00:31:42.460
but I think it was Muscle?

00:31:42.840 --> 00:31:44.960
Okay. Or one of those terrible

00:31:44.960 --> 00:31:46.680
fighting games. I think it was Tag Team Wrestling.

00:31:46.960 --> 00:31:48.160
Tag Team Wrestling. Yeah,

00:31:48.380 --> 00:31:49.420
the AI just like,

00:31:49.720 --> 00:31:51.400
was like, this is how the game works,

00:31:51.500 --> 00:31:52.820
so I'll just do it exactly the way it works.

00:31:52.900 --> 00:31:54.020
So I feel like there's a fine line

00:31:54.020 --> 00:31:54.900
between like what you're

00:31:54.900 --> 00:31:56.420
describing in Pool and that.

00:31:56.840 --> 00:31:58.480
Yeah. So I didn't play anything

00:31:58.480 --> 00:32:00.680
with the computer AI,

00:32:00.980 --> 00:32:02.240
but I was thinking

00:32:02.240 --> 00:32:03.320
the whole time

00:32:03.320 --> 00:32:04.760
that I feel like this game would really shine

00:32:04.760 --> 00:32:05.740
with a second player.

00:32:05.940 --> 00:32:07.660
Like, I feel like that's where it would be the most fun.

00:32:07.820 --> 00:32:09.280
It's kind of like the first time we played

00:32:09.280 --> 00:32:10.200
NES Golf together,

00:32:10.200 --> 00:32:11.040
though, and like,

00:32:11.140 --> 00:32:12.780
I already liked that game

00:32:12.780 --> 00:32:14.580
